meta {
  name: Get Triage Record by Derived Id
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{CRM_URL}}/rpa_integrationinboundqueues({{triageRecordId}})?$select=rpa_integrationinboundqueueid,rpa_name,rpa_errordetails,rpa_processingresult,rpa_processingentity,rpa_processingstage,statuscode,createdon,modifiedon
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  $select: rpa_integrationinboundqueueid,rpa_name,rpa_errordetails,rpa_processingresult,rpa_processingentity,rpa_processingstage,statuscode,createdon,modifiedon
}

headers {
  Prefer: odata.include-annotations="OData.Community.Display.V1.FormattedValue"
}

script:pre-request {
  // Reproduces deriveIntegrationInboundQueueRecordId in fcp-sfd-crm
  // (src/repos/crm.js): sha256 of the parts joined with ':', the first 32
  // nibbles shaped into an RFC 4122 v4 GUID.
  //
  // Read from environment variables, not from a vars:pre-request block.
  // bru.getVar reads only runtime variables; a vars:pre-request entry
  // populates request variables, a separate collection used solely for
  // {{...}} interpolation and invisible to bru.getVar. Reading them that way
  // silently yields undefined, so the derivation below would never run.
  const correlationId = bru.getEnvVar("correlationId");
  const fileId = bru.getEnvVar("fileId");
  const failureReason = bru.getEnvVar("failureReason") || "document_type_not_found";

  if (correlationId && fileId && failureReason) {
    // Required inside the branch, not at the top. require('crypto') is only
    // available in the "developer" sandbox; the default "safe" sandbox has no
    // such module and throws, which would fail the request before it is sent
    // even when the caller supplied triageRecordId and needed no derivation
    // at all.
    const crypto = require('crypto');

    const parts = ['integrationinboundqueue', correlationId, fileId, failureReason];
    const hex = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(parts.join(':')).digest('hex').slice(0, 32).split('');
    hex[12] = '4';
    hex[16] = ((parseInt(hex[16], 16) & 0x3) | 0x8).toString(16);
    const g = hex.join('');
    const id = `${g.slice(0,8)}-${g.slice(8,12)}-${g.slice(12,16)}-${g.slice(16,20)}-${g.slice(20,32)}`;
    console.log(`derived triage record id: ${id}`);
    bru.setEnvVar("triageRecordId", id);
  } else {
    console.log(`using existing triageRecordId: ${bru.getEnvVar("triageRecordId")}`);
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Fetches one triage record by its primary key, and derives that key first
  rather than looking it up.

  fcp-sfd-crm supplies the primary key on create instead of letting
  Dataverse mint one. The key is a sha256 of
  'integrationinboundqueue:{correlationId}:{fileId}:{failureReason}' shaped
  into a v4 GUID, which is what makes the write safe to repeat: the same
  failure always addresses the same record, and If-None-Match: '*' turns
  every later attempt into a 412.

  The pre-request script reproduces that derivation. Set correlationId,
  fileId and optionally failureReason as *environment* variables and it
  computes {{triageRecordId}} before the request goes out. Leave them unset to
  use whatever {{triageRecordId}} already holds, for instance the value "List
  Recent Triage Records" set from the newest row.

  They must be environment variables rather than pre-request variables.
  bru.getVar reads only runtime variables, so a vars:pre-request entry is
  invisible to it and the derivation would quietly never run.

  *Deriving here needs the developer sandbox.* require('crypto') exists only
  in that sandbox, not in the default "safe" one. In the app, set it in
  collection settings; from the CLI, pass --sandbox developer. Supplying
  triageRecordId directly needs neither, because the require sits inside the
  branch that derives.

  Verified against the deployed function: correlationId
  77777777-8888-4999-8aaa-bbbbbbbbbbbb, fileId
  cccccccc-dddd-4eee-8fff-000000000000, reason document_type_not_found
  derives f4f45052-760f-4bc7-afac-b872349cd2ac.

  Two uses. Predictively, derive the id *before* forcing a failure and
  confirm afterwards that exactly that record exists — proof the key is
  deterministic rather than incidental. Diagnostically, a 404 here when the
  logs claim the write succeeded means the id in the log's event.reference
  and the id in CRM have diverged, which would be a real defect.

  failureReason must be one of contact_not_found_for_crn,
  account_not_found_for_sbi, document_type_not_found or
  document_type_metadata_incomplete. Any other string derives a GUID for a
  record that was never written, and the request answers 404.
}
